    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Estate Agents are proud to present \"Monatrea\" a detached bungalow which occupies a prime location on the periphery of Celbridge village. This fine home offers prospective purchasers a rare opportunity to acquire a property on a wonderful secluded site which is positioned well back from the road and offers incredible privacy with large wrap around gardens providing an ideal setting.\nThis is an attractive detached family home and measures 146 sq ms. Built in 1949 the house has been well maintained over the years and is generally in good order throughout, however it would benefit from modernisation and refurbishment. This blank canvas property certainly offers the buyer the opportunity to renovate, refurbish and redecorate to their own personal style and taste.\nUpon entering, one is immediately struck by the spacious, light filled entrance hallway. There is a good sized living room, with dual aspect windows, exuding an abundance of natural light with views to the gardens, a dining room, a kitchen and a conservatory. Additionally, there are three double bedrooms & family bathroom. The large attic has been converted offering plenty of scope for extra storage.\nExternally are well appointed, landscaped gardens enjoying an abundance of maturity, seclusion and privacy from neighbouring homes. Dressed with a variety of lawn areas, colourful trees, shrubbery and plant life. To the front is a large entrance driveway providing off-street parking with access to outbuildings and sheds to the side and rear of the property.\n\"Monatrea\" is ideally located within walking distance from Celbridge village with its host of eateries, pubs and shops. Also, within close proximity of the M4/M50/M7, shopping centres, as well as a host of other amenities that include schools, public transport, parks and sporting facilities. The wonderful Castletown House and surrounding grounds are just minutes away offering plenty of space for the outdoor enthusiast to enjoy, with its markets, music and cultural events throughout the year.\nRarely does a home of this calibre and unique nature come to the market in this area and as such viewing is highly recommended.\n\n\nTo arrange a viewing call Audrey Higgins on 01 6280400"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5m x 1.68m\nCarpet flooring, alarm panel, doors to\n\nLiving Room - 4.79m x 5.87m\nDual Aspect with carpet flooring, feature brick fireplace with stove inset,\n\nDining Room - 5.30m x 3.34m\nDual aspect, with carpet flooring, sliding doors to patio/garden areas\n\nKitchen - 2.56m x 4.67m\nLaminate flooring, wall and base kitchen cupboards wooden work surfaces, tiled splash back, door to rear garden\n\nHallway - 7.67m x 1.03m\nCarpet flooring, attractive ceiling coving, doors to\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.27m x 3.41m\nSide aspect, carpet flooring, shelving, currently used as home office\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.42m x 4.01m\nSide aspect, carpet flooring, fitted wardrobes, under stair storage\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.72m x 3.65m\nRear aspect, laminate flooring,\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.15m x 1.27m\nFully tiled throughout with w.c., wash hand basin, shower cubicle with electric T90si shower\n\nFamily Bathroom - 4.95m x 1.95m\nFully tiled with heated towel rail, w.c., wash hand basin, shower cublicle\n\nConservatory - 3.7m x 3.25m\nTiled flooring doors to rear garden\n\nConvered Garage Space - 7.84m x 2.99m\nWith access from main house\n\nConverted Attic Space - 15m x 4.84m\nConverted attic space with stairway entrance offering extra storage\n\n"
      },
